1. Prerequisites

| Item | Value |

| ISO      | `rhel-9.x-x86_64-dvd.iso` from [access.redhat.com](https://access.redhat.com/downloads) |
| CPU      | 2 vCPUs |
| RAM      | 4 GB (min 2 GB) |
| Disk     | 40 GB |
| Network  | NAT (Workstation) or VM Network (ESXi) |

**Verify the ISO checksum** before use:

> sha256sum rhel-9.x-x86_64-dvd.iso

2. Create the VM

### VMware Workstation

1. **File → New Virtual Machine** → **Typical** → Next
2. **I will install the OS later** → Next
3. Guest OS: **Linux** → **Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9 64-bit** → Next
4. Name: `RHEL9-VM` → choose storage path → Next
5. Disk: **40 GB**, single file → Next
6. **Customize Hardware**:
   - Memory: **4 GB**
   - Processors: **2**
   - CD/DVD: **Use ISO image file** → browse to your RHEL 9 ISO
   - Network: **NAT** (default)
7. Click **Finish**

### VMware ESXi / vSphere

1. **New Virtual Machine** → **Create a new virtual machine**
2. Guest OS: **Linux** → **Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9 (64-bit)**
   > ⚠️ Requires **hardware version 18+** (ESXi 7.0 U3+). If not available, select **RHEL 8** as guest OS — it works fine.
3. Hardware: CPU **2**, RAM **4 GB**, Disk **40 GB** (thin)
4. CD/DVD: **Datastore ISO file** → browse to ISO → check **Connect at power on**
5. **Finish**

## 3. Boot & Install

1. **Power on** the VM
2. At the GRUB menu, select **"Install Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9"** → Enter
3. **Language**: English → **Continue**

In the **Installation Summary** screen, configure these four items:

### a) Installation Destination
- Select your virtual disk (e.g. *40 GiB VMware Virtual Disk*)
- Storage Configuration: **Automatic** (default LVM layout is fine)
- Click **Done**

> ⚠️ The disk will be **erased**. On a VM this is fine, but if you're reusing a disk with an existing OS, back up first.

### b) Software Selection
- Base Environment: **Minimal Install** (recommended) or **Server with GUI**
- Click **Done**

> ⚠️ Pick **Minimal Install** for servers. You can always add packages later with `dnf`.

### c) Network & Hostname
- Enable the network adapter (toggle ON)
- Set a hostname (e.g. `rhel9vm.local`)
- Click **Done**

### d) Root Password & User
- Set a **root password**
- Click **Create User** → enter name, username, password → check **Make this user an administrator**
- Click **Done**

> ⚠️ **Set both** root password AND an admin user. Anaconda won't warn you if you skip either — you'll be locked out.


## 4. Begin Installation

1. Click **Begin Installation**
2. Wait 5–10 minutes
3. Click **Reboot System**
4. **Detach the ISO** before it reboots (Workstation: CD/DVD → Disconnect; ESXi: uncheck *Connect at power on*)

> ⚠️ If you forget to detach the ISO, the VM will **boot back into the installer**. Just power off, detach, and power on again.

## 5. Post-Install

# Verify
uname -r          # 5.14.0-xxx.el9.x86_64
getenforce        # Enforcing
ip a              # Check IP

# Register (if you skipped during install)
subscription-manager register

# Update
dnf update -y

> ⚠️ **Don't skip registration** — without it, `dnf update` won't pull security patches.

## 6. (Optional) Install VMware Tools / Open VM Tools

sudo dnf install -y open-vm-tools
sudo systemctl enable --now vmtoolsd

This gives you **shared clipboard**, **drag-and-drop**, and **automatic display resolution** in Workstation.

That's it. Total time: ~10–15 minutes.

